          "id": "the_drive_cycle_weights_are_one_distribution_over_twenty_three_running_modes",
          "description": "W, unchanged from `process-airtoxics` and `process-crankcase-running`: one distribution per day type over the 23 operating modes `emissionratebyage` carries, summing to 1. It has no pollutant-process axis on road type 4 -- both rated blocks collapse against the same weights -- which is what makes `rtDay_meanBaseRate` a single self-contained stage per parent. The distribution's total and its mode count are no longer variables and are not asserted; what is asserted is the physics-row selection and the two braking thresholds the weights are built from.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
