        {
          "id": "the_mode_resolved_rate_reproduces_sbWeightedEmissionRateByAge",
          "description": "S13(a) against `sbweightedemissionratebyage`, the reference's own generator output, BEFORE the drive-cycle collapse. `process-airtoxics` named this table and did not read it; reading it here separates a wrong `emissionratebyage` key from a wrong W, which matters more in this rung than in any before it because the rate half runs twice and a key error on one parent alone would move five of the seven emitted blocks. operating_mode_rows is the table's own order, so mode 0 is position 1, mode 1 is 2 and mode 40 is 25. The EV-sales factor is 1 on every row -- `fleetavgadjustment` has no rows in this snapshot -- so this equals the reference column exactly rather than approximately.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "tolerance": {
            "rel": 2e-05
          },
