        {
          "id": "125_cohorts_are_selected_124_are_rated_and_every_one_of_the_seven_blocks_is_the_same_104",
          "description": "THE KEY-SET CLAIM, made in the document rather than in a comment. 1,456 rows is equally consistent with 4 x 364 and with 8 x 182, and the comparator's exact-key-set check would not separate a seven-block set from a mis-shaped one either, so the cohort count was asserted PER pollutant-process: 104 seven times, against one shared cohort set. The selected counts are 125, 125, 0, 125, 125, 125, 0 -- the two zeros are organic carbon and H2O aerosol, which MOVES never rates and for which it therefore writes no `pollutantprocessmodelyear` row, which is why the EMISSION test rides on the cohort relation. 125 - 1 rated - 20 = 104, and the 20 are lost twice over: no `sulfatefractions` fuel-9 row and no `crankcaseemissionratio` fuel-9 row. `criteriaratio` is EMPTY here and reaches 0 pairs, which is the mirror image of `process-airtoxics`, and `generalfuelratio` is live and reaches 67 (rate row, supplied formulation) pairs, every one of them on a RATED row.\n\nWHAT IS STILL ASSERTED is a sample of rate rows -- emitting rows in four blocks, four non-emitting rows, one selected and one unselected row -- and the fuel-usage wildcard count of 5. The per-pollutant-process counts, the 728 total and the reach counts are gone from the model, and `cohortSurvivorCount` now counts the cohorts the output carries (104, not 125); none of them is asserted here.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "tolerance": {
            "rel": 1e-09
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.run_fuelUsageWildcardCount",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 5.0,
              "coords": {
                "run_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
